# Version 1.4.0 - Updated dependencies, restored lights without shaderpack

## Added

- Added a dedicated depth-based light pass for Iris installations with shaderpacks disabled
- Added automatic switching between the native framebuffer pass and the Iris shaderpack pass

## Changed

- Updated compatibility for Veil 4.1.4
- Updated compatibility for Iris 1.8.14 beta 1
- Updated compatibility for Sodium 0.8.12 beta 1
- Rebalanced shaderpack light contribution to preserve block textures and material detail
- Simplified shaderpack compositing to a single controlled light pass
- Removed the secondary screen-blended fill pass introduced in 1.3.3

## Fixed

- Fixed Veil colored lights disappearing when Iris was installed but shaderpacks were disabled
- Fixed overly saturated shaderpack lighting replacing the visible texture of illuminated blocks
- Fixed a crash caused by attempting to reactivate Veil dynamic-buffer internals that Veil disables while Iris is installed

